\par\par \b \uc2  ECB Procedures, Technical Options For  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikako Mogi \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2000\par 17:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT -(Dow Jones)- If the euro's decline against the dollar and yen reaches a point at which it threatens price stability in the eurozone, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the tools in place to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the authority to use them. \par \par \uc2  The following outlines the ECB's policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possible scenarios should it choose to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  HISTORICAL ECB STANDPOINT: \par \par \uc2  The ECB has yet to show any indication that it is poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro gets battered. \par \par \uc2  The ECB has in the past said it doesn't have a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly if conducted unilaterally, would be limited. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it is carefully monitoring the euro's prolonged depreciation and expressed concern that continued euro weakness is aggravating inflation risks, coming at a time when the euro area is undergoing the best economic upswing in years. \par \par \uc2  PROCEDURES: \par \par \uc2  The eurosystem - the ECB and the 11 national central banks in the euro zone - would take a leading role in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Individual national central banks can't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on their own. \par \par \uc2  The ECB is legally under no obligation to get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approved by euro-zone finance ministers, and can decide and execute any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own. \par \par \uc2  But the Maastricht Treaty also provides finance ministers with some leeway. The Ecofin council - which consists of the finance ministers of the member states of the European Union - can conclude formal agreements on an exchange rate system for the euro and can formulate general "orientations" for exchange rate policy. They can consult with and make recommendations to the ECB on this issue. \par \par \uc2  UNILATERAL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \par \par \uc2  Given the enormous risks to the young institution's credibility if an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempt failed, and a long history of failed \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other central banks, a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is virtually out of question. \par \par \uc2  COORDINATED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \par \par \uc2  Concerted action with another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - either the Federal Reserve or the Bank of Japan - is more likely. The Bank of Japan is likely to be more forthcoming on the issue than the U.S. at this point, given the recent slew of comments by Japanese authorities expressing concerns about the euro's plunge against the yen. With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long experience in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , emerging prospects of a BOJ-ECB joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could induce a self-imposed turnaround in market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  But, importantly, the U.S. hasn't yet publicly expressed concerns about the dollar's strength against the euro. The Fed is seen as having more clout with the market and thus a longer-lasting impact on market trends than the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  TECHNICAL OPTIONS: \par \par \uc2  The ECB could place commercial euro buy orders on a bilateral basis with a commercial bank. Without coming into the open, the ECB could try to enhance market uncertainty and trigger short-covering, which could support the euro. \par \par \uc2  It could buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell the dollar outright. It could conduct swap transactions, mixing spot and futures transactions. It could operate solely through futures contracts, or it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through repurchase agreements. \par \par \uc2  But each of these direct purchases has its own limits. \par \par \uc2  Swaps and futures transactions would only have a small impact, if at all, because those markets are driven by expectations of forthcoming financial developments - something the ECB can't control. Repos neutralize the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the ECB has to engage in a reverse transaction at a later date. \par \par \uc2  STERILIZE OR UNSTERILIZE: \par \par \uc2  Unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more effective because when the ECB buys the euro, it effectively applies a restrictive monetary policy by reducing the base money circulating in the markets. Interest rates rise as available money shrinks. And higher interest rates could attract capital and could give the euro a further boost. \par \par \uc2  But the consequences of unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on price stability and money supply growth may not be positive. \par \par \uc2  If the ECB doesn't want interest rates to rise, it would have to sterilize \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying bonds and adding money back into the markets. \par \par \uc2  -By Chikako Mogi, Dow Jones Newswires; 49-69-29725-500; chikako.mogi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9704duu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
