\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  lurches pose headaches beyond euro zone borders. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 1,000 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2000\par 19:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers risk attracting the firepower of more than just the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they keep driving European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the dollar and the yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said. \par \par \uc2  While the euro's fall once more to record lows against the dollar hit the headlines again on Wednesday, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not short of company, nor is the ECB the only \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be plagued by exchange rate worries. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc crashed to 11-year lows against the dollar on Wednesday and sterling is precariously perched within a cent of seven-year troughs against the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  There are two sides to the story - while the euro is down five percent so far this year, the dollar is up five percent. \par \par \uc2  This would make it easier for the ECB to present \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges as a response to excessive dollar strength against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than an attempt to stem isolated euro weakness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  It also means the ECB could find a willing ally in the Swiss National Bank. Japan wants the dollar to strengthen against the yen but could be counted on to help in any action that would weaken the yen at least against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of England, however, is not expected to join in any action. British memories of the harrowing drama of the expulsion of sterling from Europe's exchange rate mechanism are still too fresh, even though it occurred as long ago as 1992. \par \par \uc2  "Two out of the three major economic blocs are finding domestic policy-making more difficult because of exchange rate moves and there is a responsibility, bordering on an obligation, for central banks to try and reverse this trend," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of imbalances being caused by the strong dollar and if euro zone central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the SNB might not even wait for the call to get involved." \par \par \uc2  CENTRAL BANKS YET TO DECLARE OPEN WAR \par \par \uc2  The ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  once in 1999, but has never yet been spotted acting on its own account even though the euro has shed more than a quarter of its value against the dollar. The SNB has also not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years. \par \par \uc2  But such action could be the only way to stop a slide which gathered new momentum on Wednesday, as the euro shed more than two percent to hit record lows below $0.87 and under 92 yen. The franc also tumbled two percent to near 1.78 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Central banks from euro zone countries are seen bidding for euros almost daily on electronic dealing systems, but their interest has so far been dismissed by traders as linked commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even when it occurs at critical levels. \par \par \uc2  Talk that the SNB was quietly leaking dollars onto the market has also become rife as the Swiss franc has tumbled two percent in as many days against the dollar, but again, this has not been viewed by traders as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is possible that they are selling dollars, but that would be commercial transactions," said a Zurich-based trader. \par \par \uc2  The SNB could use rhetoric to signal its displeasure at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, as it did to good effect in April when an SNB official said it was no longer trying to hold the franc stable against the euro, triggering sharp gains in the franc. \par \par \uc2  It also has the option of using monetary policy to defend the franc, as it did in March when it raised key Swiss rates by a larger-than-expected 75 basis points. \par \par \uc2  ACTIONS SPEAK LOUDER THAN WORDS \par \par \uc2  But if the ECB's experience is anything to go by, the impact of rhetoric and rate hikes soon fades when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have the bit between their teeth. \par \par \uc2  European central banks may therefore find themselves forced to show the markets the colour of their money, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "They need to put their hands in their pocket and not just issue a strongly worded communique," said Parsons at Commerzbank. "There are enough central banks with enough credibility to have a serious impact on this market." \par \par \uc2  The last time European central banks clubbed together to take on the foreign exchanges was in 1995 when the dollar was falling to record lows against a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which have now been subsumed into the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The SNB was quick to join in then as the Swiss franc's strength against the dollar was crimping economic activity. The battery of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeded in turning the dollar around and started a rally in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has yet to end. \par \par \uc2  Coordinated action now could have an equally big impact, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "If I saw the ECB and SNB come in simultaneously, I would take more notice than if it was just the ECB," said Neal Kimberley, manager, European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  The need to halt the dollar's ascent against the euro is all the greater as traders and analysts around the world report that long-term investors are beginning to switch into the dollar and the yen and out of euros. \par \par \uc2  Still, analysts said conditions may be more propitious for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than previously - a key consideration given the ECB is seen wary of the damage its credibility would suffer if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and failed to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  "It is a more desireable scenario for central banks to come in now than it was last September when the market was overweight of euros," said Richard Adams, vice president at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "I would want to see whether it triggers demand from real money investors, particularly North American ones who were the first the get bearish on the euro, before I say it is successful but I see the current moves as the endgame rather than a new phase of euro weakness." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9608qio\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
