\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Nakahira Blames Euro Weakness On ECB \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2000\par 08:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders "can't get rid of expectations that the euro will continue to fall," said Ryohei Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "It will be difficult (for the euro) to rise back above $0.9000 and I think the market will begin to search the euro's bottom," he said. "Since markets overshoot, you can't deny the possibility" that the euro will fall to Y90.00. \par \par \uc2  The market's belief that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro anytime soon is one major factor that's weighing on the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kosuke Nakahira, a former Japanese vice finance minister for international affairs, told Dow Jones Newswires that the only way for European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to stop the euro's drop is to indicate that they are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \uc2  "The euro's weakness is clearly not based on fundamentals and stems mainly from the fact that the market doesn't take euro-zone authorities very seriously because of their apparent lack of a unified policy," said Nakahira, who is currently the vice chairman of private research body Institute for International Economic Studies. \par \par \uc2  Some players, however, don't dismiss the possibility of euro-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of hand. \par \par \uc2  "If (the euro) fell rapidly, I think there's a good chance that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be conducted," Nomura Trust's Suzuki said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials, at least, hint that they would take action if the yen rises too sharply against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, the head of the Finance Ministry's international bureau, said Wednesday that the euro "should strengthen based on economic fundamentals," adding that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are closely watching moves in the euro-yen. \par \par \uc2  But some traders said that mixed signals about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy coming out of Europe suggest that an ECB-led \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  They pointed to German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's remark Monday - that the weakness of the euro "should be more reason for joy than reason for concern" when exports are considered - as evidence that euro-zone officials aren't too worried about the home \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's collapse. \par \par \uc2  "Schroeder said he welcomes euro weakness and he is the head of state, after all," said Commerzbank's Muramatsu. "The ECB will probably only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a very last resort." \par \par \uc2  While the euro has moved sharply over the past few sessions, the dollar-yen has been fairly stable. Wednesday, the dollar stayed in a narrow range between Y105.62 and Y105.95. Traders said worries that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen if the dollar fell below Y105.00 are making players reluctant to build up long yen positions. \par \par \uc2  -By Kenneth McCallum, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; ken.mccallum@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9604e30\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
