\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Mutoh: To Take Appropriate Action On  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  If Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2000\par 10:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The top bureaucrat at the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday that the ministry will take appropriate action against a too-rapid strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "A strengthening of the yen, especially a rapid strengthening, will have undesirable effects on the Japanese economy," Toshiro Mutoh told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "If necessary, we will take appropriate action (on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets)," Mutoh said, when asked about the dollar/yen's recent fall below Y106.00. \par \par \uc2  But Mutoh declined to comment on the reasons behind the yen's strengthening and current dollar/yen levels. \par \par \uc2  Market players fear MOF and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen if the dollar/yen falls below Y106.00 \par \par \uc2  Mutoh said that MOF has been watching long-term interest rates when implementing fiscal policy, and will continue to do so. \par \par \uc2  "We are aware that interest rates move according to various factors, such as monetary policy and government bond issues," Mutoh said. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to watch carefully the market mechanism in which long-term interest rates move," Mutoh said. \par \par \uc2  The top MOF bureaucrat declined to comment, however, on current long-term interest rate levels, saying only that his ministry will watch over the markets. \par \par \uc2  "But we will make sure that (interest rate movements) do not drag down (the overall economic recovery,)" Mutoh said. \par \par \uc2  -By Miyako Takebe and Hidenobu Kageyama, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com, hidenobu.kageyama@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9404d4p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
