\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro trapped near record lows, awaits U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2000\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 1 (Reuters) - The euro on Friday was pinned within one percent of the record lows it set against the dollar a day earlier amid lingering concerns that higher euro zone interest rates could harm euro zone economic growth. \par \par \uc2  At the same time there was market optimism that the U.S. economy was on course for a soft landing, which would help maintain the attractiveness of U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  Traders said caution ahead of the key U.S. non-farm payrolls and average earnings data, due at 1230 GMT, had this session helped the euro keep about half a cent away from its record lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, they added that if the U.S. data reinforced expectations of a soft landing, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably renew its decline, although any losses were expected to be limited ahead of a holiday in the U.S. on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "People are bearish on the euro and use any excuse to sell it and if the U.S. data comes in line with expectations with the market on the whole dollar bullish, the dollar could creep up," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at the Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "The only scope for the euro to rally is if we see outlandishly strong numbers or very weak numbers which lead to a reappraisal of the soft landing for the U.S.." \par \par \uc2  The euro was languishing within a yen of all-time lows around 94 yen set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro was steady around $0.89, down about 24 percent since its launch in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  It was within one percent of a record trough of $0.8837 set on Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark minimum bid rate by 25 basis points to 4.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The hawkish tone of the statement issued by the ECB after the rate move triggered speculation that more rate hikes were in the pipeline. But this was seen as a euro negative as it raised the prospect of a hard landing in the region, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen the ECB tighten and their rhetoric suggests that they are prepared to tighten again, but for that to underpin the euro we need to have good economic data and euro zone data has not been very good in recent weeks," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI. \par \par \uc2  EURO ZONE OFFICIALS' COMMENTS DISREGARDED \par \par \uc2  The euro derived little inspiration from euro-supportive comments from senior euro zone officials ahead of the U.S. data. \par \par \uc2  Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet said that there is a "flagrant" undervaluation of the euro, while the European Commission repeated that euro zone fundamentals were very healthy and it was confident that the euro will grow in the financial market. \par \par \uc2  "We had euro zone officials saying that euro zone fundamentals remain good but it has not had any impact because people seize upon bad news rather than good news," said Razia Khan, treasury economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro zone manufacturing Purchasing Managers' data, which showed that the pace of growth in the region has slowed, was also more or less overlooked by the market. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone August manufacturing PMI fell to 58.6 in August from 59.2 in July, its lowest since February. The Eurozone Prices Index dropped to 67.1 last month, its lowest since December 1999, from 72.0 in July. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted Friday was the deadline for payment for Germany's UMTS mobile phone licences recently auctioned for 100 billion euros. \par \par \uc2  While the successful bidders should have covered most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure by now, but dealers still wondered if there might be a last-minute scramble for euros. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar was trapped in tight ranges against the yen around 106.40/50, largely unmoved by a spate of comments from senior Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said he was not worried about the yen's recent strength against the dollar. The Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said BOJ monetary policy continued to support \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  economic recovery and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be carried out if necessary. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9109866\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
