\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-ECB euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  would require doggedness. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2000\par 13:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must have the stomach for a protracted fight and be assured of U.S. help if it wants to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resist the euro's fall towards record lows on the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  Concern that recovery in the euro zone might be unable to withstand the higher interest rates warranted by accelerating inflation drove the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to within one percent of record lows against the dollar and the yen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  With rate hikes seen more likely to hurt the euro than help it, the ECB may find itself having to make its first foray into the foreign exchanges on its own account to buy euros. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is guaranteed to give the foreign exchanges a short sharp shock, traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But the ECB must be ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and show it has U.S. backing if such tactics are to convince them that a decline which has seen the euro shed a quarter of its value against the dollar since its 1999 launch is finally over. \par \par \uc2  "I would take my lead from the central banks for the first 12 or 24 hours, but it would have to be concerted and continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for me to keep following it," said Eddie Tofpik, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ADM Investor Services in London. \par \par \uc2  He said he was targeting euro losses down to $0.87, about 1.5 cents below the record lows plumbed in May. \par \par \uc2  IS ECB PRUDENT OR SCARED? \par \par \uc2  Euro zone central bankers have always said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one of the weapons in their armoury, a comment reiterated as recently as Tuesday by Bundesbank council member Hans Reckers. \par \par \uc2  Back in April, German central banker Helmut Schieber offered some insight into why such action had not yet been taken when he said the ECB, whose main goal is ensure price stability, had not wanted to give the impression it had explicit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the ECB would still be keen to avoid sending such a message but could feel it had no other option given euro weakness was stoking price pressures at a time when the inflation rate was already above the ECB's self-imposed ceiling. \par \par \uc2  Other euro zone central bankers have put more emphasis on the risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not work, with several saying this year that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not work without U.S. help. \par \par \uc2  For once, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers found something they could agree on with central bankers. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to be done in collusion with the Fed to have any real sustained impact," said Neal Kimberley, manager, European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that the ECB would want the U.S. Federal Reserve at its side if it was picking a fight with the foreign exchanges were reinforced by comments in June by Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet. \par \par \uc2  At that time, Trichet said the authorities were not practicing the kind of benign neglect which had been the norm at the beginning of the 1980s and that steps could be taken if a consensus prevailed among leading industrial nations. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not have a "mechanistic efficiency" but nevertheless had been and could be used as a signal. \par \par \uc2  The case for the U.S. to get involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own account could be growing given the dollar's gains against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have boosted it to its strongest in a decade on trade-weighted measures, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But even if other members of the G7 come to the ECB's aid, it could take more than a one-off foray into the foreign exchanges to engineer a sustained euro rally. \par \par \uc2  The ECB would have to match the doggedness of the Japanese authorities, who repeatedly sold yen between June 1999 and April 2000 to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-crippling strength in check, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been successful but it threw extremely large amounts of money at the problem, and this is something Europe and the U.S. have never been prepared to do," said Adrian Schmidt, international economist at Chase Investment Bank in London. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8n0aqwg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
