\par\par \b \uc2  Yen seen having more to lose than gain post BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2000\par 13:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The risks for the yen are skewed to the downside as it heads into Friday's nail-biting Bank of Japan policy meeting following a war of words between the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japanese politicians. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have gone a long way to pricing in the risk of the first Japanese rate rise in nearly a decade as Governor Masaru Hayami said this week he would like to take the earliest opportunity to end the zero-rate policy and stuck to his guns in the face of massed political opposition. \par \par \uc2  The yen's ability to surf much higher than the three-week highs of 107.50 per dollar it has set on Thursday is expected to be limited if the BOJ delivers a rate rise, even though the majority of economists are betting on no move. \par \par \uc2  But losses the yen would suffer if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its fire could be much bigger, not least because the intense political pressure put on the BOJ to keep monetary policy unchanged has raised the stakes in financial markets' eyes. \par \par \uc2  "The yen has got pretty much all the mileage it is going to out of the prospect of a rate rise," said Adrian Schmidt, international economist at Chase Investment Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "If we don't get one, it would not be a disaster, but given that Hayami has nailed his colours to the mast, it would get people thinking that the BOJ is being influenced by politics or, at the least, that he does not have control of the committee." \par \par \uc2  He said he was expecting the yen to enjoy no more than fleeting gains if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates but predicted the dollar would rally half a yen immediately if it left policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  NO END TO YEN'S IMPRISONMENT \par \par \uc2  Whatever the outcome of the BOJ's meeting, analysts said they did not expect the yen to break out of the ranges it has been caged in against the dollar for nearly a year with the help of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exchanges. \par \par \uc2  Gains the dollar would make if the BOJ left monetary policy unchanged on Friday were unlikely to take it past the two-month highs near 109.80 which were tested on three successive days about two weeks ago, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "We would see yen selling on a decision to leave rates unchanged but I would not expect the dollar to get much beyond 109 given that at the end of the day we will get a rate hike in the months ahead," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Commerzbank Asset Management in London. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, even a 25 basis point hike in Japanese interest rates would not be enough to trigger a rally which could take the yen past 106, not least because such a move would raise concern about Japan's fledgling economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  This would still leave the Y 4.5 percent weaker than the four-year highs it hit against the dollar in November 1999. \par \par \uc2  This would also be well away from any danger zone that might prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell yen on the foreign exchanges, as it has done on at least 17 occasions since June 1999. \par \par \uc2  "Even if we get a move from the BOJ, it is hard to see the dollar moving below 106.50 and I don't see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks at all given the last time we had any such talk was when the dollar was below 105,"said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in London. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8a00885\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
