\par\par \b \uc2  Japan spent Y1.385 trln in Apr-June to boost dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2000\par 02:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Monday it spent 1.3854 trillion yen during the April-to-June quarter on dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  All of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place on April 3, it said. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time the ministry explicitly indicated a figure for spending on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ministry said it would continue to release such data on a quarterly basis. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts as MOF's agent in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has intermittently stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last year to prevent a rapid appreciation of the yen against the dollar, which Japanese authorities fear may choke of the tentative economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell sharply in late March and threatened to break through the closely watched 100 yen per dollar mark, but since the April 3 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the yen has largely held within a 103 to 110 yen per dollar range. On Monday morning it was quoted at 108.65/68 to the dollar. ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8700sic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
