\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Releases  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Data For First Time \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2000\par 08:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry released data about its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time ever Monday, bowing to pressure to be less secretive about its market activities. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said that during the April-June quarter, Japan conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  once on April 3, selling Y1.385 trillion of yen for dollars in an effort to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That action, taken when the dollar was trading around Y103.50, caused the dollar to jump more than two yen during Tokyo trading, eventually pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of Y105.62, traders said at the time. \par \par \uc2  The release of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data represents an abrupt turnaround in policy for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, who have long refused to reveal any details about the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless doing so directly served their own policy purposes. In general, ministry officials have said that such information is a state secret and that releasing details on the subject to the public could undermine the effectiveness of future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A ministry official said Monday that the release of the data on a quarterly basis follows Japan's new policy of releasing more information about how it manages its foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  From April, the ministry began to announce a whole slew of additional information about its reserves, such as the specific amount of gold and foreign securities it holds, in order to follow International Monetary Fund guidelines on disclosing reserves data. \par \par \uc2  "We're in the age of information disclosure, so we're going in the right direction by actively revealing" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, said Toshiro Mutoh, administrative vice finance minister. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities of other industrialized countries, such as the Federal Reserve, already publicize \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data. Aware of this global trend, ministry officials had held discussions for months with counterparts in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which conducts actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on orders from the ministry. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "The Most Information We Could Release"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It's no accident that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lagged other countries in publicizing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data. Ministry officials had long maintained that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par situation is different from its counterparts when it comes to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in yen trading needs to be conducted more\par frequently because exchange rate moves have a bigger impact on a major\par trading economy like Japan's compared with other economies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Therefore, they maintained, facts about the way \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par should be kept secret to the extent possible. In some cases, news\par agencies that reported \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by confirming the action with\par anonymous sources have later received phone calls from authorities in\par Tokyo who politely but persistently tried to find the source of the\par leak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even with the new information, the ministry will retain some degree of\par secrecy. For example, the ministry's new data list only the day that\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was conducted, the total amount of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair that was traded.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There's no mention of specific levels where the action was taken.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is the most information that we could release, when considering\par that we have to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effective," the ministry official\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vice finance minister Mutoh said: "If it emerges that (revealing too\par much information about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) has a negative impact, we would\par have to consider how to publicize (the data) in a way" that would\par prevent such problems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders shrugged off the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data: the\par amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in April-June was in line with market estimates\par and the data were too old to have any effect on current trading, they\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Unless the ministry announces the scale immediately after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the announcement won't affect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels,"\par said Kazuki Fujita, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at the Industrial\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But in the long run, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data have the potential to change\par the way that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  carries out its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. Some BOJ officials\par have said that historically, yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has had only a\par short-term impact on exchange rates and has often paradoxically caused\par yen strengthening to accelerate down the line.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By showing that money spent for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has often had\par the opposite of its desired effect in the long-term, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data\par could make \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less prone to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so often, those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par officials said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (The Finance Ministry's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data are available on\par the Internet at\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mof.go.jp/english/files.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mof.go.jp/english/files.htm}}}\uc2 \f2 )\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Kenneth McCallum, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par ken.mccallum@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1135 4201 55129 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw8703u2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
