\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Distances Itself From  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention Operations \highlight\uc2 ; Policy Clue? \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2000\par 02:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Who calls the shots on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? \par \par \uc2  For the record, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't - the Finance Ministry does. That's the message in an article the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted on its website two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  "In our country, the finance minister has jurisdiction over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance minister makes decisions on the implementation, timing and amount," the BOJ said. "As an agent of the finance minister, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on the finance minister's instructions." \par \par \uc2  Just another helpful public service reminder? \par \par \uc2  Maybe, maybe not. \par \par \uc2  Here's one theory: the BOJ aims to avoid sending mixed messages on policy. The idea is that a rate hike here could cause a knee-jerk strengthening of the yen. The Finance Ministry has made it clear it would counter a rapid rise in the yen with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is carried out by the BOJ, there is a risk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would appear to be conducting two contradictory policies at once. \par \par \uc2  In this sense, the BOJ's effort to distance itself from the decision-making process in regard to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seem to be one more sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preparing to tighten policy - maybe as soon as July 17, when the policy board meets next. \par \par \uc2  "The main point is that (the BOJ) would like to separate the discussion of the termination of the zero interest rate policy from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Hiromichi Shirakawa, chief economist at UBS Warburg in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Before joining UBS Warburg last year, Shirakawa spent 16 years as a career BOJ official, most recently managing the research team in the money and capital markets division in the BOJ's financial markets department. \par \par \uc2  For its part, the BOJ denies any ulterior motives. "We want to explain the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," A BOJ spokesman said. "There is no policy motivation, none at all," he added. \par \par \uc2  But analysts note that anyone who might care about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably already knows that finance ministry officials direct that policy. That's why journalists so often seek comment from ministry officials regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  It wouldn't be the first time the BOJ has used its website to drop subtle hints about its intentions on monetary policy, Shirakawa said. \par \par \uc2  Just over a month ago, the BOJ released a research paper on the asset price bubble and monetary policy in which the authors - both senior BOJ officials - pointed out the negative effects from keeping monetary policy loose for too long a decade ago. The paper enhanced speculation that the BOJ is growing more concerned about the risk of repeating the same mistake with its zero-rate policy and is therefore eager to normalize monetary policy as soon as possible. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; arran.scott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7703bfb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
