\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Edges Up Against Euro, Ends Lower Against Yen Ahead Of Tankan Survey \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2000\par 14:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar finished mixed in quiet trading Monday ahead of the Independence Day holiday in the U.S. and a key survey of Japanese business sentiment due out Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the euro was quoted at 95.03 U.S. cents, down from 95.30 U.S. cents late Friday in New York. The dollar was quoted at 105.66 yen, down from 105.97 yen late Friday in New York. The pound fetched $1.5130, down from $1.5172 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar weakened a bit in New York following the release of the National Association of Purchasing Managers June business index, which fell to 51.8 in June from 53.2 in May. The figure was considerably lower than the reading of 53 expected by Wall Street analysts and was the lowest reading since 49.9 in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The data provided fodder for those who believe the Federal Reserve's interest-rate increases are coming to an end. The euro, which had been trading below 95 cents, managed to breach that level following the release of the NAPM survey. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded in a very tight range against the yen, with participants reluctant to make bold moves ahead of the release of the quarterly tankan survey of business sentiment, scheduled for release Tuesday morning in Japan. The survey is expected to show a 2.7% rise in Japanese business sentiment, which could prompt the Bank of Japan to abandon its near-zero interest-rate policy, perhaps at its next meeting on July 17. Higher interest rates would make yen-denominated assets more attractive for investors. \par \par \uc2  A strong tankan report and expectations for higher interest rates in Japan could push the dollar lower against the yen, but traders said if the dollar falls to around 104.50 yen to 104 yen, it could prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ and (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) have tended to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on announcement days," said Robert Sinche, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Citibank in New York. "And tankan has been catalyst before for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so I wouldn't rule it out at all." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the purchasing managers index for the euro zone showed some slowing in the pace of growth since the ECB raise its short-term interest rates by an aggressive half a percentage point on June 8, bolstering expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold rates steady when it meets Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The PMI, which measures activity in the euro zone's manufacturing sector, slipped slightly in June to 59.5 from 59.7 in May. \par \par \uc2  The pound, meanwhile, fell amid anticipation that the Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee will hold rates steady when it meets Thursday. The latest PMI data out of the United Kingdom showed the lowest level of manufacturing growth there in nearly a year. The seasonally adjusted PMI fell to 50.2 in June from 50.8 in May. Analysts' forecasts were for the index to come in at 50.6. A reading above 50 indicates expansion, while a sub-50 number points to a slowdown. \par \par \uc2  Finally, the Mexican peso rallied following the stunning victory of opposition candidate Vicente Fox in Sunday's presidential elections. Late Monday, the dollar was quoted at 9.5700 pesos, down from 9.8350 pesos at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  (Compiled from Dow Jones Newswires and other sources) \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2000 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020330dw7301fyv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
