\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sustains gains against dollar, yen rebounds. \b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2000\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In LONDON, June 30 story headlined "\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Euro sustains gains against dollar, yen rebounds", please read in first paragraph...The euro held most of its gains against the dollar...instead of... against the euro (corrects \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). \par \par \uc2  A corrected story follows. \par \par \uc2  (Updates with fresh quotes, latest prices) \par \par \uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 30 (Reuters) - The euro held most of its gains against the dollar having rising to 10-day highs earlier on Friday, buoyed by expectations that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase interest rates further out. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the yen recovered from earlier weakness against the dollar amid speculation that next week's tankan business sentiment survey will allow the Bank of Japan to end its zero-interest rate policy at its July 17 meeting. \par \par \uc2  The euro was bolstered after the release of French producer price and Italian industrial orders, the latest in a string of stronger-than-expected euro zone economic data, which helped reinforce euro zone rate hike expectations. \par \par \uc2  "Data we've had over the past couple of days have indidated that economic momentum is strong, inflation is still creeping higher and the risk is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to raise rates," said Teis Knuthsen, chief strategist at SEB Merchant Banking in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/dollar is ticking higher but it is within ranges we've seen before and we really need to see break above $0.97. Only then can we turn somewhat more bullish." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading within a half cent of its $0.9601 10-day peak by 1143 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The overall French PPI index rose 1.3 percent on the month in May for a year-on-year increase of 11.4 percent. Even after excluding the volatile energy and food prices, the index was up 2.5 percent on the year. \par \par \uc2  Italian April industrial orders rose an unadjusted 15.9 percent year-on-year compared with a rise of 7.5 percent in March. \par \par \uc2  The rally in euro/dollar was accompanied by talk that a European national \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying euros for commercial purposes. The Bundesbank declined to comment on the rumours. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said with the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting out of the way and had produced no change in U.S. interest rates, as expected, the focus had returned to the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "It seems realistic to admit that the end of the U.S. hike is near," said Gilles Borrel, head of global treasury sales at Westdeutsche Landesbank in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "There's still some leeway on the upside on the European side, so the euro, mechanically, should improve." \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise earlier took it to 10-day highs against sterling at 63.45 pence and against the yen at 101.11. Since then those gains have been pared. \par \par \uc2  YEN AWAITS TANKAN \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that despite a softer tone for the yen after Fitch's downgrade of Japan's domestic debt on Thursday, the outlook for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely be bullish for the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Indeed the yen had rebounded around one yen against the dollar from troughs around 105.70 set earlier on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We are going into a very significant month for Japan," said Knuthsen at SEB. \par \par \uc2  The new government is to hold its first parliamentary session next week and the tankan quarterly business sentiement survey will be released. \par \par \uc2  In the following days Japan will host the Group of Seven meeting of finance ministers and later in the month the Bank of Japan will hold its regular policy meeting, at which there are some market expectations interest rates could be raised. \par \par \uc2  "Over the next couple of weeks the pressure will be for dollar/yen to move lower, with a limit at around 103 which will be hard to break as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be seen as at least threatening to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Knuthsen said. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44 20 7542 7792, fax +44 20 7542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1211 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -\tab \tab \tab     Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1999\par -\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  29 Jun\tab \tab \tab   Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.9556   0.9517   +0.41    -5.10   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab    105.20   105.23   -0.03    +2.93   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab   100.49   100.20   +0.29    -2.53   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.6295   1.6352   -0.35    +2.47   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.5103   1.5180   -0.51    -6.63   1.6176\par Dlr/cad\tab \tab    1.4810   1.4821   -0.07    +2.46   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.6010   0.6016   -0.10    -8.43   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5575   1.5570   +0.03    -2.87   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6327   0.6264   +1.01    +1.41   0.6239\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6u02i58\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
