\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Soggy as Fed watch intensifies. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 1,151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2000\par 10:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 23 (Reuters) - Pre-weekend caution and Wall \par \par \uc2  Street's losses dampened interest in Asian stocks on Friday as \par \par \uc2  investors hunkered down ahead of the Federal Reserve's ruling \par \par \uc2  on interest rates next week. \par \par \uc2      Most economists polled by Reuters expect the Fed to leave \par \par \uc2  short-term rates unchanged at the June 27-28 meeting, but many \par \par \uc2  expect a quarter point hike at the August meeting. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong markets -- the most vulnerable to a U.S. rate \par \par \uc2  hike due to the territory's dollar peg -- lost ground, though \par \par \uc2  volumes were low. \par \par \uc2      Japan's Nikkei average also ended lower ahead of Sunday's \par \par \uc2  general election, while Taipei shares were hurt by losses on \par \par \uc2  the Nasdaq and news China had scheduled live firing exercises \par \par \uc2  in the Taiwan Strait. \par \par \uc2      JAPAN AWAITS POLL \par \par \uc2      Tokyo stocks gave way to wariness ahead of the election, \par \par \uc2  but many analysts expect the market to head higher once the \par \par \uc2  poll is out of the way. \par \par \uc2      Newspaper surveys this week have forecast the ruling \par \par \uc2  coalition led by the Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) will retain \par \par \uc2  its majority, but analysts noted that the outcome was hard to \par \par \uc2  predict, with half the electorate still unsure about their \par \par \uc2  vote. \par \par \uc2      And there was little optimism that the winner of Sunday's \par \par \uc2  poll would produce a new blueprint to tackle the problems still \par \par \uc2  plaguing Japan's fragile recovery. \par \par \uc2      "The LDP has done a pretty poor job of managing the economy \par \par \uc2  recently and is showing an increasing tendency to back away \par \par \uc2  from the painful structural changes that are necessary for \par \par \uc2  Japan to improve its growth rate long-term," Bank of America \par \par \uc2  said in a research note. \par \par \uc2      The yen faltered as Japanese officials kept alive the \par \par \uc2  threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot to a two-month \par \par \uc2  high of 104.12 against the dollar overnight. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced a quandary as any \par \par \uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be at odds with its increasingly \par \par \uc2  loud rhetoric favouring an end to the zero rate policy. \par \par \uc2      HYUNDAI HOPES \par \par \uc2      Korean blue chips sagged after Wall Street's fall, but \par \par \uc2  shares in the Hyundai Group were higher on news of 900 billion \par \par \uc2  won in investment into its financial units. \par \par \uc2      The group's shares were also lifted by reports \par \par \uc2  DaimlerChrysler was set to take a 10 percent stake in Hyundai \par \par \uc2  Motor The Korean car firm's shares rose 4.3 percent to 16,900 \par \par \uc2  won. \par \par \uc2      The German car giant said it would outline its alliance \par \par \uc2  with Hyundai at a joint news conference in Seoul on Monday. \par \par \uc2      The won gave way to foreign fund sales of Korean shares, \par \par \uc2  but chartists said the dollar seemed to have found a short-term \par \par \uc2  top at 1,122 won. \par \par \uc2      KOREA REVISES FORECASTS \par \par \uc2      Investors were uninspired by Korea's upward revision to its \par \par \uc2  2000 growth forecast as the figure was in line with what many \par \par \uc2  analysts had been predicting in any case. \par \par \uc2      The ministry said it expected the economy to grow eight \par \par \uc2  percent, instead of the six percent predicted earlier, as \par \par \uc2  strong exports, infrastructure investment and the activity of \par \par \uc2  start-up companies offset still sluggish domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  "I think the government initially was very, very \par \par \uc2  conservative. Six percent was an unrealistic figure," said \par \par \uc2  Bhanu Baweja, regional economist at IDEAglobal.com. \par \par \uc2      "Even as the momentum slows, I think nine percent is quite \par \par \uc2  achievable," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      Inflation was also expected to be fairly subdued, with the \par \par \uc2  ministry trimming its CPI forecast to 2.0-2.5 percent from an \par \par \uc2  earlier projection of three percent. \par \par \uc2      The current account surplus is now expected to be $10-$12 \par \par \uc2  billion for the year, from a previous estimate of $12 billion. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SAGA \par \par \uc2      The rift between Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and President \par \par \uc2  Abdurrahman Wahid's government rumbled on, keeping the rupiah \par \par \uc2  under the gun, though acting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Anwar Nasution \par \par \uc2  did sound a somewhat reassuring note. \par \par \uc2  The senior deputy governor, who is heading Bank Indonesia \par \par \uc2  while its chief is under detention, said he would stick to \par \par \uc2  reforms agreed with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to stick to the 'road map' and pledge to \par \par \uc2  implement it more vigorously," he told Reuters, adding that BI \par \par \uc2  would pay special attention to restructuring banks and helping \par \par \uc2  them cope with liquidity problems. \par \par \uc2      There have been concerns that BI governor Sjahril Sabirin's \par \par \uc2  detention would slow the restructuring of the ailing sector. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the removal of Sabirin over his suspected \par \par \uc2  involvement in a banking scandal had also sparked concern that \par \par \uc2  Wahid might replace him with someone more pliable. \par \par \uc2      But Baweja of IDEAglobal.com was more upbeat, pointing to \par \par \uc2  Sabirin's ties with former president Suharto as a negative. \par \par \uc2      "Wahid has in the past been pretty consistently whittling \par \par \uc2  down Suharto's old order and I think this is another step in \par \par \uc2  the same direction," he said. \par \par \uc2      "So I see this as a positive. Rupiah downside should be \par \par \uc2  seen as a buy opportunity in the long term." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0818 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     104.41\tab  105.25\tab    +0.80\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7312\tab  1.7346\tab    +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    30.767\tab  30.778\tab    +0.04\par  Korean won   1119.00\tab 1118.50\tab    -0.04\par  Baht\tab      39.07\tab   39.17\tab    +0.26\par  Peso\tab      42.85\tab   42.86\tab    +0.02\par  Rupiah\tab  8676.00\tab 8680.00\tab    +0.05\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     104.41\tab  102.21\tab    -2.11\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7312\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.88\par  Taiwan dlr    30.767\tab  31.380\tab    +1.99\par  Korean won   1119.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +1.43\par  Baht\tab      39.07\tab   37.45\tab    -4.15\par  Peso\tab      42.85\tab   40.20\tab    -6.18\par  Rupiah\tab  8676.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -19.61\par  Rin