\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen retains firm tone amid rate speculation. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 22 (Reuters) - The yen rose against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday benefiting from persistent speculation about an end to Japan's zero-rate policy in July although fears of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited its gains. \par \par \uc2  The rate hike view was reinforced by comments from the BOJ Deputy Governor Sakuya Fujiwara who, earlier in Asia, reiterated the bank's belief that an end to deflation fears was near. \par \par \uc2  However, the market remained wary of breaking through the 105.00 level in dollar/yen, concerned that it may trigger BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen's industry-crippling strength since Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa specifically mentioned it during a press conference a few weeks ago, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is still in the spotlight and not far from Miyazawa's ceiling of 105," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market attention is focused on Fujiwara's comments and that is keeping the zero-rate policy in the spotlight and there is plenty of event risk in the pipeline but much will depend on elections on Sunday." \par \par \uc2  The yen was hovering near day's highs around 105.20 against the dollar. It is about two-percent above last week's low of 107.15 yen. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen retested Wednesday's three-week lows around 99.40 yen. It is down more than three percent from 103.00 highs seen just a week ago. \par \par \uc2  "They are trying very strongly to get this idea discounted in the market. It looks like they really are very serious about a change," Marshall Gittler, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk at Bank of America in Tokyo, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "Furthermore, an increasing body of sentiment says maybe as early as the July meeting," he added. \par \par \uc2  EURO SUPPORTED AROUND $0.9375 \par \par \uc2  Traders also reported talk that foreign investors were buying Japanese equities, in part because recent upbeat data had restored their confidence in the Japanese recovery and partly due to lessened political risk ahead of Sunday's general election. \par \par \uc2  A spate of opinion polls suggest the ruling coalition is likely to gain a stable majority at the poll, so avoiding any policy uncertainty that could result if a little-tried opposition party were to take power. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was holding below the key $0.9500 level in the wake of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaving rates on hold on Wednesday and European officials recently hinting that euro-zone rates were likely to remain on hold until Autumn. \par \par \uc2  The euro was pegged with half a cent of its Wednesday's two-week lows around $0.9430, down about three percent from two-month high of $0.9701 scaled on June 8. Traders said the euro remained unsettled due to uncertainty about what the Federal Reserve would do at next week's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The market has been assuming that recent soft data would keep the Fed on hold, but economists at the respected American Bankers Association on Wednesday predicted it would indeed hike next week because growth was not slowing enough. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also note that overall monetary conditions in the United States have eased in recent weeks as markets bet the tightening cycle was near to finishing. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly the ECB has hinted that rates will remain on hold until September," said MacKinnon at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is suffering from temporary fatigue from the rally we saw from around $0.8840 (record lows hit mid-May) but there is very good support at $0.9375, which I expect to hold." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6m02zto\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
