market. It looks like they really are very serious about a change," Marshall Gittler, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk at Bank of America in Tokyo, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "Furthermore, an increasing body of sentiment says maybe as early as the July meeting," he added. \par \par \uc2  EURO SUPPORTED AROUND $0.9375 \par \par \uc2  Traders also reported talk that foreign investors were buying Japanese equities, in part because recent upbeat data had restored their confidence in the Japanese recovery and partly due to lessened political risk ahead of Sunday's general election. \par \par \uc2  A spate of opinion polls suggest the ruling coalition is likely to gain a stable majority at the poll, so avoiding any policy uncertainty that could result if a little-tried opposition party were to take power. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was holding below the key $0.9500 level in the wake of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaving rates on hold on Wednesday and European officials recently hinting that euro-zone rates were likely to remain on hold until Autumn. \par \par \uc2  The euro was pegged with half a cent of its Wednesday's two-week lows around $0.9430, down about three percent from two-month high of $0.9701 scaled on June 8. Traders said the euro remained unsettled due to uncertainty about what the Federal Reserve would do at next week's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The market has been assuming that recent soft data would keep the Fed on hold, but economists at the respected American Bankers Association on Wednesday predicted it would indeed hike next week because growth was not slowing enough. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also note that overall monetary conditions in the United States have eased in recent weeks as markets bet the tightening cycle was near to finishing. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly the ECB has hinted that rates will remain on hold until September," said MacKinnon at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is suffering from temporary fatigue from the rally we saw from around $0.8840 (record lows hit mid-May) but there is very good support at $0.9375, which I expect to hold." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6m02zs7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
