\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Options - Dlr/yen vols surge up on break of 105. \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 22:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, June 22 (Reuters) - Implied volatility in dollar/yen options surged higher on Thursday as the dollar plummeted through 105 yen on prospects for an improved Japanese economic outlook and easing fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen slid to 104.12 early in New York trading hours and was hanging near 104.50 late as front-end implied volatility jumped sharply and the back end bumped higher also. \par \par \uc2  Yen also jumped against the euro, with implied volatility bouncing higher in euro/yen options also, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "They did move up quite a lot," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options trader said. "We took out the 105 and took out the barriers and are facing prospects of further yen strength, so the market is a little anxious." \par \par \uc2  However, the market does not appear especially concerned that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the yen rise, traders said. Traders seem more bent on giving up long dollar positions than holding out for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Sakuya Fujiwara said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawing closer to ending its unprecedented easy monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/yen implied volatility jumped to 13.1/13.4 percent from near 12.1/12.4 percent early. One-year implied volatility firmed to 14.0/14.2 percent from 13.7/13.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The one-month dollar/yen risk reversal firmed to 2.6/2.9 or a touch higher from a mid of about 2.5 at the open. \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/yen implied volatility popped up to 14.8/15.25 percent from 13.9/14.3 percent early in the day. One-year implied volatility bounced to 15.3/15.55 from 15.15/15.4 percent at the open. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar implied volatility also started to get a little more bid as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to below 93.50 cents in New York hours and remained well below 94.00 cents late. \par \par \uc2  The market was "a little more anxious, more interested in buying the downside today than we have seen for a while," one trader said. The market has tried and failed to work the euro from the long side for the 18 months of its existence. \par \par \uc2  One-month implied volatility in euro/dollar firmed to 12.25/12.5 percent, up about 0.20 of a vol higher from the morning, and the one-year rose marginally from early morning to 12.8/13.0 percent. ((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6m02zox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
