\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : BOJ Fujiwara Speech Drags Dlr Down Against Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 07:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Another sign that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is accelerating its drive for a credit tightening sparked dollar selling for yen in Asia Thursday, sending the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower compared with its levels in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained almost flat against the dollar because of a dearth of new trading factors. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by the Bank of Japan's Deputy Governor Sakuya Fujiwara caught \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players off guard, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In a clear sign of his shift to a hawkish policy stance from the neutral, Fujiwara said in a speech that "the policy board's discussion on ending the zero-interest rate policy is coming close to a conclusion," and "even if the zero-rate policy were to be abandoned, that would not mean that the monetary policy has entered a tightening cycle." \par \par \uc2  Since Fujiwara spoke only three days after a hawkish policy comment by another BOJ deputy governor, Yutaka Yamaguchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players took Fujiwara's words as more proof that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has begun seriously considering ending the policy as early as possible, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Fujiwara's remarks was a reprise of Yamaguchi's comment three days ago. It was clearly aimed at laying the groundwork for terminating the policy," said Yasunari Ueno, chief economist at Fuji Securities. \par \par \uc2  After Fujiwara spoke, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players rushed to sell dollars for yen in anticipation of higher Japanese interest rates, sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as low as Y105.18 at one point. Around the level, however, the dollar was supported by fears of dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y105.18, below Y105.61 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.38 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9467, slightly higher than $0.9458 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9513 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In a press conference after his speech, Fujiwara reiterated his hawkish stance. Fujiwara said that the BOJ cannot continue its zero-rate policy forever, since it was adopted as an "emergency measure" to prevent a deflationary spiral. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that Fujiwara repeated the hawkish stance indicates the BOJ's drive for an early abandonment of the zero-rate policy is accelerating," said Ryuichi Takami, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market didn't respond to Fujiwara's repeated message in the press conference. However, since market speculation is rising that the BOJ will abandon the policy early, and a substantial amount of dollar-selling orders for loss-cut has been placed around Y105.00, the dollar will eventually go down to low-Y104 levels in the coming week, market players predicted. \par \par \uc2  Though the euro managed to maintain Wednesday's closing level in New York, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside remains soft, dealers said. Some still hold euro-long positions accumulated during its rise to $0.9701 two weeks ago, they noted. Moreover, warnings by European monetary officials against a euro fall are growing less frequent, and this is also contributing to its downward momentum, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "European officials appear to be less concerned about the euro these days. The euro could fall near to $0.9300 again in coming weeks," said Takami. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y99.57, down from Y99.89 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y100.25 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5018, up from $1.4993 in New York but lower than $1.5141 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Takeshi Takeuchi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par -0- 22/06/00 06-40G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6m031v7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
