\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Break Below Y105 Not Seen Causing BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Christine Richard \par \uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2000\par 18:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar's sustained break below Y105 Thursday won't result in any immediate action from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to U.S.-based analysts. \par \par \uc2  Any form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the remainder of the U.S. session is deemed highly unlikely and the response during Friday's Asian trading could limited to jawboning from the usual BOJ or \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, said analysts. \par \par \uc2  But opinions are mixed on the significance of move under Y105, considered by many as the BoJ's "line in the sand" against a strong yen. \par \par \uc2  "There is the risk of BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Paul Podolsky, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at FleetBoston. "It's likely we'll at least see verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later tonight." \par \par \uc2  Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Pittsburgh-based Mellon Bank, said that there was little chance of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ clearly isn't protecting certain levels," said Chandler. "Also, speculative forces may not be all that long yen. The yen buying is from fund managers and Japanese exporters hedging, so the speculative market isn't going to be caught very long." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has held in a tight range versus the yen of Y105-Y107 for the last two weeks with dealers describing the Y105 level  Earlier Thursday the pair touched a low of Y104.14 though it had retraced slightly to around Y104.46 as of 12:25 p.m. (1625 GMT). \par \par \uc2  "There were an unusual number of stop losses at Y104.80, Y104.50 and Y104.25," said John Schein, vice president at Fortis, noting that this type of buying pressure is unlikely to be seen as a major threat by the BoJ. \par \par \uc2  Schein said, however, that a break through the next major support of Y103.85 would be a different story. A determined push below that level would increase the chances of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The last time the BoJ directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was on April 17 when the dollar hit Y103.30. \par \par \uc2  If there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is most likley to come in the euro/yen market, said Dan Bernzweig, a trader at Bank Leumi. "Euro/yen is the convenient place to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it would be well-received given (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) officials want to see the euro stronger." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But generally, the yen is seen having a bit more leeway on the upside,\par analysts said.\par -By Christine Richard, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4384;\par  christine.richard@dowjones.com\par  (Tom Barkley contributed to this article)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010804dw6m00fhj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
