\par\par \b \uc2  Euro seen vulnerable as yen bulls seek easy prey. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2000\par 13:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 21 (Reuters) - The path of least resistance for those wanting to bet on a stronger yen is to buy the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for euros rather than dollars, heightening the risk of a broad euro setback, analysts said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Demand for yen has mounted in recent weeks amid speculation Japan's economic recovery may be strong enough to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soon end its 16-month old policy of keeping interest rates pinned near zero. \par \par \uc2  Japan is expected to resist any significant export-crippling yen gains by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges as it has done at least four times already this year. But it is seen mainly concerned with keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the weaker side of 105 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders appear inclined therefore to express yen bullishness by buying the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for euros, particularly since the euro is already displaying signs of fatigue after sprinting higher for a month. \par \par \uc2  The euro plumbed three-week lows against the yen on Wednesday and more such pressure could see a rerun of the events of last year when its losses against a resurgent yen compounded its woes against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro does have that sinking feeling to it again but part of the problem is that in a sense it is suffering through no fault of its own," said Keith Lewis, manager, treasury markets at American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is emitting all the signs that it is going to strengthen, so we could see euro/yen do the damage again and turn out to be one of the early warning signals that the euro is back in the doldrums." \par \par \uc2  But Lewis said the euro's fate was still finely balanced, given that the recent ranges which have caged both it and the yen against the dollar are still intact. \par \par \uc2  The euro was mired near the bottom of the $0.9450 to $0.97 range which has prevailed for the past two weeks, with the dollar holding half a yen above the floor of the 105 to 107 yen band which has kept it trapped during that time. \par \par \uc2  EURO SEEN A SOFT TARGET \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as easy prey since a steady stream of upbeat economic reports from the 11-nation euro zone has failed to resuscitate a rally which had taken it to two-month highs against the dollar and yen earlier in June. \par \par \uc2  Germany's closely watched Ifo business climate survey and Italian growth numbers released on Tuesday were both stronger than expected but failed to lift the euro's spirits. \par \par \uc2  By contrast, optimism about the yen and the Japanese economy is proving resilient to patches of bad news, such as the weaker-than-expected Japanese all-industries index released on Wednesday. "There is a certain sense of disappointment that the euro has not made much progress on the strong data we had yesterday and there has been a subtle mood shift," said Mark Cliffe, international economist, ING Barings in London. \par \par \uc2  "Given the Japanese story and the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of dollar/yen, euro/yen is a cautious way to put on a trade." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen at least 17 times since June 1999 but on all bar one or two of those occasions it has sold yen for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Economists are therefore not expecting any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen and said it could cede more ground to the yen. However, few are as yet looking for a retest of the record lows below 95 yen and $0.8850 which the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plumbed in May. \par \par \uc2  "I would not expect any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen and we could see the euro go down towards 95 (yen)," said Adrian Schmidt, economist at Chase Investment Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "This is just a correction and I would not expect a move down to new (record) lows." \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 20 7542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6l035vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
