\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen favoured on recovery outlook, euro flagging. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2000\par 05:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - The yen was well-supported in late morning trade on Wednesday as the market's upbeat view on Japan's recovery prospects weathered some soft economic indicators. \par \par \uc2  But its progress against the dollar was hampered, with fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) resurfacing every time it nears 105 yen to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 105.54/64 yen, having slipped as low as 105.21 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 105.53 yen in U.S. trading on Tuesday. The euro maintained a softer tone against the yen and the dollar, unable to extend gains on a solid German Ifo survey overnight. \par \par \uc2  The euro was weighed down when European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg indicated interest rates would be steady for some months to come, although inflationary risks still linger. The euro floundered at $0.9513, compared with $0.9543 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen , the euro probed lower to 100.41 yen, having slipped from 101.35 yen in late Tokyo on Tuesday. It closed at 100.84 yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment remained bullish (on the yen) as the recovery is still intact, " said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Japanese data on Wednesday morning were softer than expected with the all-industries index down 0.2 percent month-on-month in April, while the tertiary sector index dropped 0.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  The indices are seen as key clues to GDP for the quarter, but analysts wrote off the April weakness as a payback for exceptional strength in March. \par \par \uc2  "The pace in service sector activity may be a bit slower, but I have not detected signs that the slowdown will continue. Overall, economic activity is gradually recovering," said Jun Inoue, economist at Fuji Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  Also released was Japan's May trade surplus data, which came in at 582 billion yen, well below market expectations. But again this was balanced by U.S. trade figures overnight showing the deficit with Japan hit a record $7.3 billion in April. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also noted Japan's imports rose a robust 19 percent on the year, pointing to an improvement in domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  Yen bulls were also seeking clues to whether the BOJ will abandon its zero interest-rate policy as early as next month. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ is expected to closely watch summer bonuses, as they want to see incomes stabilise before ending the zero-rate policy. \par \par \uc2  A survey by the business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun showed summer bonuses this year averaged 1.16 percent higher than in 1999, making the first rise in two summers. \par \par \uc2  The yen's momentum has been bolstered since the Economic Planning Agency's (EPA) latest monthly report, released on Tuesday, upgraded its assessment of Japan's economy as expected. \par \par \uc2  Crucial to the interest rate outlook will be the BOJ's quarterly "tankan" survey of business sentiment due on July 4, which analysts expect to show further improvement. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said foreigners are actively selling dollars in anticipation of a victory by the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's coalition in Japan's general election on Sunday. "They will probably cover their short positions to take profits, after confirming the expected victory by the LDP," one said, predicting the yen would retreat on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In morning trading, the euro succumbed to pressure from profit-taking to edge lower, hitting stop-loss orders at $0.9520. The euro was only briefly boosted overnight after the release of the German Ifo survey index. The closely watched figure surged to 102.1 in May, its highest level since March 1991, outstripping the average market forecast for a rise to 101.4. \par \par \uc2  But the euro's gains were short-lived, in part because rumours ciculating in the market prior to the Ifo's release had suggested it would be even higher. ((Tokyo Treasury desk +81-3 3432-8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0326 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 20 Jun.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab  0.9510   0.9543   -0.35   -5.56   1.0070\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab   105.47   105.53   -0.06   +3.19   102.21\par Euro/yen\tab \tab  100.31   100.84   -0.53   -2.71   103.10\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab 1.6320   1.6283   +0.23   +2.63   1.5902\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab   1.5137   1.5176   -0.26   -6.42   1.6176\par Dlr/can\tab \tab   1.4710   1.4706   +0.03   +1.76   1.4455\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab   0.5987   0.6023   -0.60   -8.78   0.6563\par Euro/swiss\tab      1.5528   1.5545   -0.11   -3.17   1.6036\par Euro/stg\tab \tab  0.6278   0.6287   -0.14   +0.63   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6l034uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
