\par\par \b \uc2  Euro sags vs yen, dollar as sentiment sours. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 985 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2000\par 09:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - The euro fell against the dollar and the yen on Wednesday as sentiment soured in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to break above a key resistance level earlier this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid to a three-week low against the yen and was mired near $0.95 in late afternoon trade, despite data released overnight showing an improvement in German business sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro may suffer further in the near term, with more stop-loss offers said to lurk below $0.95, but they were more upbeat on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's medium-term prospects. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is taking a breather after a recent rally," said Takayuki Togawa, manager for Tokai Bank, who said the euro could test $0.93 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  But Togawa thinks the trend of capital flows into the euro zone and away from U.S. asset markets remains intact, amid concern of a slowdown in the U.S. economy, adding the euro's declines are likely to be short-lived. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped against the yen, dragged down indirectly by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength against the euro, but jitters about potential yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  lent the dollar some support, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was unlikely to garner support from a meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governing council later in the day, which is widely expected to keep interest rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $0.9520/25 and 100.15/33 yen as of 0612 GMT against $0.9543 and 100.84 yen in late U.S. trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 105.26/31 yen against 105.53 yen in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro's intraday low as of 0617 GMT was 100.08 yen, its lowest level since May 31. But they said there was less chance of a sharp rise in the yen led by falls in the euro because euro-selling by Japanese exporters and investors seemed to have passed its peak. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese institutions were able to take care of their short-term yen-buying needs when the euro rose above 102 yen earlier this month, and are now waiting to sell (the euro) at 104-105 yen to the euro," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said economic data released on Wednesday had little impact on the yen. \par \par \uc2  An all-industries index released by the Ministry of International Trade and Industry showed that Japanese economic activity contracted by 0.2 percent in April from the previous month. While the data was not weak enough to raise doubts about Japan's recovery prospects, it was not strong enough to justify buying yen actively at current levels, especially since the possibility of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can not be ruled out, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0639 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab      20 Jun.\par \tab \tab \tab   -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Euro/dlr   0.9516   0.9543   -0.28    -5.50   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Dlr/yen    105.30   105.53   -0.22    +3.02   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \