\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Down Slightly Vs Yen In Rangebound Trade \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2000\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Two emotions - hope and fear - dominated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Rising hopes that Japan's economy is about to stage a sustainable recovery vied with fears that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , clamping the dollar into a tight range. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, the latter gained the upper hand. After the dollar touched an intraday low of Y105.39 - dangerously close to the Y105 line Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa warned traders not to cross two weeks ago - traders turned tail and covered short positions. \par \par \uc2  That buying helped to lift the dollar steadily to an intraday high of Y105.65. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside was capped at that level by offers from U.S. funds and Japanese investors aiming to buy a piece of Japan's recovery as well as hedge against the risk of a stronger yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  That selling in turn bumped the dollar off its highs and helped push it below its levels late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that Japan's economy has turned a corner have been stoked by a series of upbeat economic data and increasingly optimistic comments by Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, Japanese monetary authorities have made it clear that they won't sit on their hands if the yen appreciates sharply. For instance, Zembei Mizoguchi, international bureau chief at the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reiterated his view Wednesday that the yen is too strong now. \par \par \uc2  Kenneth Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Tokyo, said Japan's economic recovery, coinciding with a slight slowdown in U.S. economic growth, means that the yen is heading higher. The dollar could fall through Y105 "at any time," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, there are growing expectations that Japan is in a sustainable recovery," Landon said. "When you get a recovery like that, demand for a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes up." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y105.38, below Y105.43 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.58 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9513, lower than $0.9574 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9582 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring growing optimism towards Japan's economy, stock prices and interest rates headed higher. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei 225 stock average ended Wednesday's session at 17210.08, up 302.53 points from the previous day's close. The yield on the benchmark 10-year Japanese government bond rose to 1.675% from 1.650 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Ryohei Muramatsu, treasury manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo, said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players are setting their sights on the Y105 level. \par \par \uc2  "The market is just considering how it's going to break through Miyazawa's ceiling," Muramatsu said. "It's just a matter of time, especially since interest rates are rising." \par \par \uc2  Muramatsu and other traders said market players will likely test the dollar's downside later in the global session when concerns about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally recede. \par \par \uc2  Below Y105.00, the dollar will likely find support at Y104.30, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Still, traders are cautious, as the BOJ would probably take action to curb the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength Wednesday was most clearly reflected in the euro's slide against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro fell steadily throughout the session, eventually touching an intraday low of Y100.09. \par \par \uc2  The mainly factor driving that move was demand for the yen from Japanese and overseas investors hedging against further yen appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "I think there was real demand too," Muramatsu added. \par \par \uc2  The euro is expected to find firm support around Y100.00. The next chart point lies at Y99.90, dealers said, with further support at Y98.60. \par \par \uc2  The euro also suffered against the dollar Wednesday, though much of the weakness stemmed from the euro's weakness against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at Y100.25, down from Y100.94 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y101.16 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5141, down from $1.5192 in New York but higher than $1.5115 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott; 813-5255-2929; Dow Jones Newswires; arran.scott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6l030c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex