\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen bolstered but BOJ fears limit gains for now. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2000\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates throughout, adds fresh quotes, latest prices, changes dateline, byline) \par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 20 (Reuters) - The yen was boosted against the euro and the dollar on Tuesday by prospects for Japan's economic recovery, but analysts said the market was wary of extending gains too far for fear the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was firmer against the dollar ahead of the German Ifo business confidence survey with talk in the market that it could come in above expectations. \par \par \uc2  Demand for yen was stimulated by comments from Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami which were bullish on the economy. He told economic ministers that the recovery was becoming clearer. \par \par \uc2  "From here on we would like to see how certain the corporate recovery becomes and to what extent this spreads into the household sector," an Economic Planning Agency (EPA) official quoted Hayami as saying. \par \par \uc2  "In general the overall downtrend in dollar/yen completely makes sense," said Tony Norfield, head of global treasury research at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen started moving lower yesterday and there have been more discussions about ending the zero interest rate policy, with the EPA (Economic Planning Agency) coming out with a more upbeat view of economic recovery." \par \par \uc2  The yen was close to a 12-day peak against the dollar hit earlier at around 105.50 . It got to around 105 earlier this month but has not been below that level since mid-April. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the yen had firmed more than 0.5 percent on the day to around 100.96 . \par \par \uc2  Still, analysts warned the market would be reluctant to push dollar/yen below 105 given the risk that the BOJ could step in to stem the rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Dealers think Japanese authorities will show strong resolve to prevent the dollar from falling below 105 yen ahead of Japan's general elections," said Taisuke Tanaka, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Credit Suisse First Boston in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda stressed on Tuesday that there was no need for a stronger yen based on current fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "Although the Japanese economy is recovering, if you look at economic fundamentals among Japan, the United States and Europe, there is absolutely no need for the yen to rise," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yen won a boost late on Monday when BOJ Deputy Governor Yutaka Yamaguchi spoke of a "full tide" for the ending of the zero-rate policy. \par \par \uc2  There was some speculation that the BOJ may decide to raise the target on the key overnight call rate to 0.25 percent from the current 0.02 percent as early as its Policy Board Meeting on July 17. \par \par \uc2  But some government officials appeared uncomfortable with an early credit move by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  EPA Minister Taichi Sakaiya said on Tuesday that next month would be too soon for the BOJ to stop pushing interest rates virtually to zero. \par \par \uc2  Norfield at ABN said U.S. April trade data due at 1230 GMT on Tuesday could add to the weakness in dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  "The trade deficit is with Asia rather than with Europe, so the risk for on dollar/yen is on the downside," he said. \par \par \uc2  MARKET AWAITS IFO SURVEY \par \par \uc2  Ahead of the U.S. data, the market will focus on the German May Ifo index at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expect a rise to 101.4, a nine-year high for the index, from 101.2 in April. \par \par \uc2  The euro had firmed around half a cent to its day's highs above $0.96 amid rumours that the index could come in above expectations. \par \par \uc2  "Disappointment here could be doubly negative for the euro by influencing expectations for next week's (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) variable rate repo)," said analysts at Bank of America in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6k032il\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
