\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar keeps upper hand ahead of U.S. PPI. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2000\par 14:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 9 (Reuters) - The dollar held firm against the yen on Friday after weaker-than-expected first quarter Japanese economic growth and consolidated near its day's highs against the euro before the release of U.S. producer prices data. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its refinancing rate by a larger than expected 50 points on Thursday and switched to a variable rate. But since it indicated this may be the last rise for a while, the focus has shifted back to the U.S. rate outlook. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the jury is out on whether the U.S. economy was slowing down enough to justify the Federal Reserve leaving rates on hold this month and would therefore be watching the U.S. producer prices data, due out at 1230 GMT for further clues. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was poised to recoup lost ground against the euro if the PPI data indicated that inflation remained a threat and rekindled expectations of a U.S. hike in June. \par \par \uc2  "Last week's U.S. data suggested that the economy was slowing down significantly and that the Fed may be on hold for now, therefore euro/dollar was bouncing ahead as people revised U.S. and euro zone interest rate differential," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI in London. \par \par \uc2  "But now the ECB rates look to be on hold for the next two, three, months and the risk is that we could see a reversal of last week's move if the PPI came strong and a 0.5 percent rise would make people think that there is a reasonable chance of a 25 point rate hike in June." \par \par \uc2  He said even if the PPI rose 0.3 percent, in line with market expectations, it would be enough to send warning signals. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was hovering 1-1/2 cents above two-month low of $0.9701 EUR=). It had fallen nearly 10 percent from its record highs around $0.8840 hit against the euro on May 19 as investors scaled back expectations of further rate hikes in the U.S. and looked for a rate hike by the ECB. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro's pull back on Thursday was partly due to concerns that the ECB's aggressive rate hike could choke-off the euro-zone's burgeoning growth. \par \par \uc2  Such worries were highlighted by the Portuguese Prime Minister Antonio Guterres who said, late on Thursday, the rate hike was unnecessary and would not help economic growth in Europe. \par \par \uc2  YEN DENTED AFTER GDP DATA \par \par \uc2  The dollar was just below a day's high of 106.72 yen JPY=), up about 1.5 percent from its seven-week low of 104.98 set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's gross domestic product grew 2.4 percent in the January-March quarter, the strongest growth in four years, but weaker than a median forecast of 2.9 percent in a Reuters poll of economists. \par \par \uc2  For the fiscal year ended in March, GDP rose 0.5 percent, falling just short of the government's target of 0.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The numbers were not too bad, but the yen didn't benefit, because after two quarters of negative growth the market wanted a clear sign that Japan is out of technical recession," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said capital spending and personal consumption were above government expectations, and the government may revise upward its 1.0 percent growth target for the 2000/01 fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was deriving support from wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's industry-crippling upside. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda and his deputy Zembei Mizoguchi repeated on Friday that Japan was ready to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed. \par \par \uc2  While the euro was struggling against the dollar, it was benefiting against the yen EURJPY=) from wider interest rate differentials between the euro zone and Japan. \par \par \uc2  Traders said in addition to weaker than expected Japanese GDP numbers, the ECB refinancing rate increase to 4.25 percent was also pressuring the yen as the euro zone and Japan rate gap widened in favour of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6903vmx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
