\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Options - Major dollar pair vols soften again. \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2000\par 21:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, June 9 (Reuters) - Implied volatility in major dollar pairs was weaker Friday in quiet spot activity as players took into account the erosion values will experience over the weekend, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility in one-month euro/dollar was quoted near 13.5/14.0 percent Friday afternoon, compared to 13.85/14.15 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Vol weakness was attributed to time decay due to the weekend, as well as the range-bound activity in spot. \par \par \uc2  Options traders crushed volatility after the euro failed to hang on to the rally over 96.00 cents Thursday and the sell-off persisted Friday. \par \par \uc2  One-month implied vols tumbled back toward the bottom of the six-week range, encompassing roughly 13 to 15 percent, on the inability of the euro to break out to the upside. \par \par \uc2  The euro was weaker against the dollar Friday following Thursday's 50-basis-point rate hike by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The move was too aggressive and hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility in one-year euro/dollar was also weaker, at about 12.95/13.25 percent late Friday, versus 13.2/13.4 percent Thursday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Despite the weakness in the euro, one-month 25-delta risk reversals were steady at about 0.5/0.8 premium euro calls. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility in one-month dollar/yen was weaker as well as spot rallied back toward the midpoint of the 105/110 trading range that has defined activity since late April. \par \par \uc2  A break out of that range was needed to force a pop in volatility, traders said. However, this was said to be unlikely as continued threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have capped yen rally attempts. \par \par \uc2  One-month implied volatility in dollar/yen was down to about 12.25/12.50 percent Friday afternoon, compared to 12.9/13.2 percent Thursday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  One-year implied vol was also softer at 13.5/14.0 percent, versus 13.85/14.15 percent late Thursday. One-month 25-delta risk reversals softened a tad to 1.8/1.95 favouring yen calls amid a quiet trade. \par \par \uc2  The yen was weaker against the dollar Friday following weaker than expected Japanese growth, hovering near 106.75 in late New York trade, compared to Thursday's 106.03 settlement. \par \par \uc2  Japanese gross domestic product for the January-March quarter rose 2.4 percent, compared to forecasts of a 2.9 rise. However, the growth was the strongest in four years. \par \par \uc2  ((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750 chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6903uxv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
