\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar finds support vs yen on Japan GDP. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2000\par 09:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 9 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the yen on Friday as slightly weaker than expected first quarter Japanese gross domestic product data dented the yen's recent bullish tone. \par \par \uc2  Japan's economy grew 2.4 percent in the January-March quarter, the strongest growth in four years, but worse than a median forecast of 2.9 percent in a Reuters poll of economists. \par \par \uc2  For the fiscal year ended in March, GDP rose 0.5 percent, falling just short of the government's target of 0.6 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The numbers were not too bad, but the yen didn't benefit, because after two quarters of negative growth the market wanted a clear sign that Japan is out of technical recession," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said capital spending and personal consumption were above government expectations, and the government may revise upward its 1.0 percent growth target for the fiscal 2000/01 year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around its highs of 106.60 at 0730 GMT, its strongest levels since Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was likely to be trapped in a range against the yen, searching for more information on the Japanese economy but wary of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's industry-crippling upside. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda and his deputy Zembei Mizoguchi repeated on Friday that Japan was ready to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed. \par \par \uc2  Market wariness about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities intensified after Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Wednesday he thought the market was aware it would be difficult to push the dollar under 105 yen. \par \par \uc2  EURO GROWTH ANXIETY \par \par \uc2  The euro struggled 1-1/2 cents below two-month highs set on Thursday in the immediate aftermath of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to raise interest rates by 50 basis points and switch to variable rate money market auctions. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said concern that the rate rise might choke off burgeoning euro-zone growth undermined the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Portuguese Prime Minister Antonio Guterres said late on Thursday the rate hike was unnecessary and would not help economic growth in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The jury was out as to the extent of a slowdown in U.S. growth, they added, putting further euro gains into question. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still in a position where it needs more information," said Gerard Gardner, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  "The question is how quickly the U.S. is coming off - I still think the Fed will hike rates." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve holds it next policy-setting meeting on June 27 and 28. \par \par \uc2  Out of 27 primary dealers of U.S. government securities surveyed by Reuters last week, only four expected the Fed to raise rates this month. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading around $0.9550 at 0730 GMT, against highs set on Thursday at $0.9701. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44 20 7542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6903u86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
