\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro broadly underpinned, eyes ECB rate decision. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2000\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 8 (Reuters) - The euro was well supported across the board on Thursday, gearing up for a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting later in the day which is expected to deliver a rate hike and possibly switch to a variable repo rate. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said strong money supply growth, strengthening growth and inflation risks provided the ideal background for a monetary tightening in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Out of 60 economist polled by Reuters all but five said they expected the ECB's key refinancing rate to be lifted by a quarter percentage point to 4.0 percent, thus narrowing the current 50 basis point gap between euro zone and U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  The ECB governing council's decision will be followed by a news conference at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "This is probably the first time in months the ECB can raise rates without hurting the euro because there are substantial signs of economic strength in Euroland, while the first cracks are beginning to appear in the U.S.," said Teis Knutsen, chief strategist at SEB Merchant Banking in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "People now are somewhat more likely to buy into the argument of a relative strong performance for the euro zone in economic terms." \par \par \uc2  By 0945 GMT the euro was holding ground near $0.9580/90, within 1/2 cent of seven-week highs around $0.9630 it set a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The euro also made headway against sterling, firming to five-month peak of 63.30 pence and it was bolstered in the mid 101s against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  RISKS OF A SWITCH TO VARIABLE ECB RATE \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the euro to resume its recent rally against the dollar if the ECB decides to switch to a variable repo rate for the current fixed system at its meeting. \par \par \uc2  The possibility of such a move had been swirling around the market already ahead of recent ECB policy meetings. \par \par \uc2  But market speculation was rife after a report in the Financial Times Deutschland on Thursday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably opt for a modified system of variable rate refinancing tenders and cited sources close to the ECB. \par \par \uc2  A variable rate would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to solve the current overbidding problem which has made it difficult for smaller bank to obtain funds. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the market has fully priced in a switch to a variable repo rate," said a trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "So we might have a spike up in the euro." \par \par \uc2  The euro showed little reaction to German unemployment figures despite a seasonally-adjusted 27,000-unit fall for May as the data had been already leaked. \par \par \uc2  Signs of improvement in the euro zone's economic outlook have sparked a near nine-percent rally in euro/dollar from record lows around $0.8845 it set in May, which could mean that some consolidation was due. \par \par \uc2  "Over the last three weeks we have seen a very big rally in euro/dollar and momentum is clearly slowing here if you look at the size of the daily moves here," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas in Paris. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen trimmed Wednesday's gains to seven-week peaks against the dollar amid wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to curb yen strength. Still, yen losses were seen limited ahead of Japanese first quarter GDP data later in the week. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading within one yen of lows around 105 set on Wednesday, its lowest since April 20. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda and his deputy Zembei Mizoguchi both took the opportunity to give a warning to the market, saying Japan would take appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Their remarks followed comments from Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa on Wednesday that he thought the market was aware it would be difficult to push the dollar under 105 yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw68040ri\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
