\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rallies after aggressive ECB rate hike. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2000\par 14:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 8 (Reuters) - The euro jumped more than 1/2 a cent on Thursday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised dealers by hiking key interest rates half a percentage point and saying it would switch to a variable refi rate from June 28. \par \par \uc2  The euro rallied to two-month highs around $0.9690 after the ECB said it had lifted its key refinancing rate to 4.25 percent from 3.75 percent, narrowing the interest rate differential between euro zone and U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose to seven-month peaks above 63.60 pence against sterling by 1210 GMT and soared to day's highs above 102.30 yen. Analysts said strong money supply growth, strengthening growth and inflation risks provided the ideal background for a monetary tightening in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  But dealers were taken aback as a Reuters survey on Thursday showed that all 22 economists polled expected only a quarter percentage point hike and showed they were split on whether the ECB would change the way it sets rates. \par \par \uc2  "We got a larger than expected rate hike in the first place and the move to a variable rate refi will also lead to higher rates," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro breaks $0.9700/50, we can see parity sooner than people expected." \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to eight-week lows against the Swiss franc after the ECB rate announcement, tracking losses against the euro. The Swiss National Bank said it had left key interest rates unchanged for now and would provide more information at its mid-year news conference next week. \par \par \uc2  The ECB governing council's decision will be followed by a news conference at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the conference will be keenly watched for hints about the direction of rates in the euro zone in the coming months, which has become a driving factor for the single currrency. \par \par \uc2  "This was a perfect time for the ECB to do more than what the market had expected because the euro was already in an upward trend," said Joanne Collins, senior economist at Daiwa SBCM Europe in London. \par \par \uc2  "We are probably going to see further euro appreciation and this move should provide underlying support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the euro to continue to be bolstered against the dollar given the ECB's decision to switch to a variable repo rate for the current fixed system at its meeting. \par \par \uc2  The possibility of such a move had been swirling around the market already ahead of recent ECB policy meetings. \par \par \uc2  But market speculation was rife after a report in the Financial Times Deutschland on Thursday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably opt for a modified system of variable rate refinancing tenders and cited sources close to the ECB. \par \par \uc2  A variable rate would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to solve the current overbidding problem which has made it difficult for smaller bank to obtain funds. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, the euro had shown little reaction to German unemployment figures despite a seasonally-adjusted 27,000 fall for May as the data had been already leaked. \par \par \uc2  Signs of improvement in the euro zone's economic outlook have sparked a near nine-percent rally in euro/dollar from record lows around $0.8845 it set in May. \par \par \uc2  "Over the last three weeks we have seen a very big rally in euro/dollar and momentum is clearly slowing here if you look at the size of the daily moves here," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas in Paris. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen trimmed Wednesday's gains to seven-week peaks against the dollar amid wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  Yen losses were seen limited ahead of Japanese first quarter GDP data later in the week. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading within 1/2 yen of lows around 105 set on Wednesday, its lowest since April 20. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets 020 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw68040dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
