\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Early 'Sell-The-Fact' Move Pushes Euro-Dlr  Down \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2000\par 07:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro failed to sustain itself above 96 cents Thursday in Asia as early "sell-on-the-fact" euro disposal set in ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recovered some of its overnight losses against the yen as traders bought dollars to cover their short positions before the release Friday morning local time of Japan's latest gross domestic product data. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players have already started factoring in the ECB's widely expected credit-tightening, dealers said. "Sell-on-the-fact" sentiment has gripped their minds, prompting them to get rid of their euro holdings ahead of the ECB's actual decision, they noted. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players finished factoring the ECB's likely rate hike of 25 basis points yesterday. The job remaining for them now is selling to take profits on the fact," said Minoru Shioiri, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Kokusai Securities. \par \par \uc2  The decisive majority of 25 banks surveyed by Dow Jones forecast that the ECB policy board members will raise the refinancing rate by 25 basis points to 4%. \par \par \uc2  But the recent improvement in market sentiment toward the euro is likely to support its downside, dealers said. The euro's fall will likely stop at around $0.9500 after the ECB's decision, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The worst period for the euro may be over by now. Even if the interest-differential factor, which pushed up the euro for the past week, is gone, a substantial euro fall is unlikely," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN AMRO Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), The euro was at $0.9592, lower than $0.9617 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9542 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at Y105.57, above Y105.45 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.88 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y101.26, down from Y101.41 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y100.90 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Though Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players on Thursday bought back the dollar for yen partly as a backlash reaction to Wednesday's intense selling, they will test a new dollar downside on Friday, dealers said. The widely expected strong showing of the January-March GDP data due out Friday morning (2350 GMT Thursday) could trigger active dollar sales, and perhaps push the dollar below Y105, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The growth rate is now expected to surpass an annualized rate of 10%. If the actual figure turns out so, market players will at least try to push the dollar below Y105.00," said Kokusai Securities' Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Dow Jones forecast on average that the economy had grown at 2.8% quarter-on-quarter. \par \par \uc2  But fear of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will support the dollar around that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Finance Minister (Kiichi) Miyazawa's words yesterday were a de facto proclamation of Japan's readiness for action once the dollar falls below Y105.00," said ABN AMRO's Takano. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said Wednesday that "the market is well aware of the fact that the Y105-wall is very high for the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The dollar could fall even further below Y105.00 if the expected high economic growth prompts the BOJ to end its current zero-interest rate policy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If the BOJ ends the policy, the dollar could fall to Y100. But such move would also drag Japan's stock prices and affect the Japanese economy. I think the BOJ can't take the action on the GDP data alone," said Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5190, down from $1.5227 in New York and lower than $1.5257 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2929; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par -0- 08/06/00 06-29G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6802t67\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
