\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides on view US may lose interest rate edge. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Sternoff \par \uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2000\par 19:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 6 (Reuters) - The dollar crumbled on Tuesdayto its lowest levels in nearly two months against major European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen, battered by sentiment a cooling U.S. economy will temper Federal Reserve interest rate hikes. \par \par \uc2  Perceived shifts in global growth and interest rates came to a head as solid economic data from Europe boosted prospects euro zone rates will rise this week, and expectations built that Japan will post healthy growth at the start of 2000. \par \par \uc2  The euro blasted to a seven-week peak of 96.01 cents EUR=) in U.S. trade, convincing traders the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge of more than 8 percent from record lows in just over two weeks was more than a last-gasp push higher. \par \par \uc2  "I think just about everybody would agree that the euro has found at least a mid-term bottom," said John Hazelton, trader at PNC Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc and British pound followed suit, pushing to respective seven-and four-week highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen, already firm ahead of a key economic growth report due Friday, then trumped all others with a fierce rally of more than 1.5 percent to a six-week peak of 105.20 JPY=) as it set off waves of technical stop-loss orders. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later pulled off its lows in early afternoon as traders took profits from the sharp market moves. \par \par \uc2  "We have a trend toward softer numbers out of the U.S. and still pretty strong numbers out of Europe. People are thinking the U.S. may be near the end of its interest cycle while Europe remains in the middle of theirs," said Eric Nickerson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  INTEREST RATES SEEN DIVERGING \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to hike its 3.75 percent refi rate this Thursday, an outlook bolstered as a euro zone consumer confidence indicator hit record highs in May and Germany's May business activity services index hit its highest level since October 1997. \par \par \uc2  A spate of soft U.S. economic reports, capped by a surprisingly weak May employment report on Friday, has traders upping the odds the Federal reserve will hold U.S. rates steady at 6.50 percent in June. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Federal Reserve Governor Edward Kelley said Tuesday a rise in the jobless rate could mark the start of a soft economic landing, but cautioned the Fed wondered whether the jobless report contained "anomalies". \par \par \uc2  San Francisco Fed President Robert Parry, meanwhile, said U.S. spending had cooled, but he did not see U.S. inflation pressures easing. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's dollar pessimism may be premature. \par \par \uc2  "Markets tend to overreact in either direction and we are seeing the overreaction snap back against the dollar," said Ben Strauss, vice president at Bank Julius Baer. \par \par \uc2  YEN EYES GDP REPORT \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  emphatically erased losses from last week that had been triggered by the failure of a Japanese life insurer and fresh concerns about Japan's financial health. \par \par \uc2  The yen burst as high as 105.20 JPY=), gaining more than 2 yen from its overnight lows, and breaking into territory which had traders newly cautious the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may wish to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem export-crippling yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "This is contrary to where the Japanese would like to see it," said PNC's Hazelton. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a Japanese bank said the yen was bolstered by some last-minute positioning ahead of a key Japanese gross domestic product report due on Friday, expected to show signs of economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast Japanese GDP will show year-on-year growth of 2.1 percent for the January-March quarter, after a sharp 1.4 percent contraction in the previous quarter. A 2.4 percent gain is required to meet the government's 1999/00 0.6 percent growth target. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw660437l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
