\par\par \b \uc2  Miyazawa says hasn't heard of Merrill  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  ban. \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 02:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 2 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Friday he had not heard of Merrill Lynch's banking arm being barred from executing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders. "I can say that I don't know about it," Miyazawa told a regular news conference. "I haven't heard about it." \par \par \uc2  Market sources told Reuters on Thursday that Tokyo authorities took action after discovering the Tokyo branch of Merrill Lynch Capital Markets Bank allegedly leaked information about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted through the bank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are decided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and carried out by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The Ministry and Merrill Lynch earlier declined to comment. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw62042fb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
