\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Cuts Merrill Lynch From  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  List-Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 06:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan have removed the Tokyo branch of Merrill Lynch Capital Markets Bank from the list of designated banks assisting Japanese authorities with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported in its Friday evening edition, citing sources familiar with the matter. \par \par \uc2  The move comes amid growing allegations that the branch leaked information concerning market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to group companies. It was removed from the list in late March, toward the end of last fiscal year, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The branch allegedly leaked information on the timing and size of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to group companies in breach of confidentiality\par obligations, the business daily reported.\par -0- 02/06/00 04-40G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6202qfq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
