\par\par \b \uc2  Merrill seen smarting from Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  allegations. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2000\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 1 (Reuters) - U.S. bank Merrill Lynch will suffer if it is long excluded by Japan from the privy circle of banks allowed to execute its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  business, London bankers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market sources in Asia earlier said Japan's Finance Ministry recently began excluding the bank from executing such orders. \par \par \uc2  The move was said to have come after the discovery that the Tokyo branch of Merrill Lynch Capital Markets had allegedly leaked information about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted through the bank to other Merrill group companies. \par \par \uc2  Key clients, like leveraged funds, may now go elsewhere to get their hands on such key market-moving information in a business where being a few seconds ahead of the pack can mean millions of dollars in profits, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, allegations that client confidentiality was breached never does a bank any good, bankers in London said. \par \par \uc2  Still, Japan can hardly hope to prevent such details getting out into the foreign exchanges given the number of other banks involved in such official transactions and the premium placed on such information, dealers in London said. \par \par \uc2  "It does matter as Merrill are now out of the loop and people like the leveraged funds who would have gone to them for this sort sort of information will go to someone else," said one London-based banker. \par \par \uc2  "But there will always be someone people can go to who will tell them what is going on. Every bank will say that they don't do it and that they protect client confidentiality but every marketer and spot dealer has an incentive to leverage off the information." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as an agent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and by issuing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buy and sell orders to banks with which it has signed contractual agreements. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  via electronic broking systems. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimate that several dozens of Japanese and foreign banks are eligible to take such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders. \par \par \uc2  The Tokyo branch of Merrill Lynch Capital Markets Bank, the banking arm of U.S.-based Merrill Lynch, was said by the market sources in Asia to have leaked information including levels at which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place and the amounts of money involved. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Ministry officials in Tokyo said they could not comment on the issue. Merrill Lynch group also declined to comment on the matter. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  EASY TO SPOT \par \par \uc2  Covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying and selling of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not always easy to spot and may sometimes be presented as commercial business but this is not the case with overt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the authorities are usually trying to throw their weight around. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen on at least 17 different occasions between June 1999 and April 2000 as Japan battled to curb the industry-crippling strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from derailing a nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The speed and size of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves usually immediately flags that such overt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being conducted. The levels at which a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealt and the approximate amounts involved typically filter through the foreign exchanges within an hour or so. \par \par \uc2  "The point with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does want people to know it has happened," said a London-based dealer familiar with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities. \par \par \uc2  "It's not great publicity for Merrill but everyone does it." \par \par \uc2  Other industrial powers have tried in the past to clamp down on leaks of sensitive information related to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to little avail. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said this was only to be expected and that it was likely the speed with which such information was disseminated, the timing of the leaks, or the way in which it was done that was likely to have triggered the action. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody does it, but it may have been a case of someone doing it in a very unsubtle way or bragging about it, in which case you are going to get caught," said a banker in London. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw61041kn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
