\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ conducted no  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  in May-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2000\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 31 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) conducted no dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in May, after spending around $13.2 billion to cap the yen's rise against the dollar in April, bankers in Tokyo said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Wednesday by the BOJ showed that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) received no payments from the private sector in May through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Net fund outflows from MOF, in the form of payments from the special account to the private sector, are often viewed as evidence of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the MOF conducts through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the net fund inflow into the special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account in May showed that the BOJ did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen this month, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data includes the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of this month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. \par \par \uc2  In April, the MOF paid 1.386 trillion yen to the private sector through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which bankers said was an indication that the BOJ had spent about $13.2 billion to support the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was last detected conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 3. The MOF confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the BOJ that day to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan has spent around $28.82 billion so far this year through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen's rise against the dollar and euro. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as the government's agent for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conducts the actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through transactions with brokers and private banks. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5v04emd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
