\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Flat Vs Yen; Risk To The Downside \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar tracked sideways across computer screens in Asia Wednesday but many traders said the risk is to the downside against the yen in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  Market players in Tokyo are becoming ever more concerned about the outlook for U.S. equities markets - and those jitters are translating into a growing aversion to holding dollars. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's 120-point fall in the Dow Jones Industrial Average and the 200-point slide in the Nasdaq Composite Index only reinforced those worries. Many Japanese investors expect that further losses are likely down the line, given expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve hasn't yet finished its current rate hike cycle. \par \par \uc2  "The decline in stocks is a matter for concern for the dollar," said Ryohei Muramatsu, treasury manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. "There is a growing feeling that one can't buy the dollar in the medium to long term. That's making the dollar heavy and creating expectations that the yen is going to appreciate." \par \par \uc2  Traders said that U.S. funds are offering the dollar between Y106.60-Y106.70, putting a firm cap on the upside. Interbank players are offering the dollar just above those levels. Technical resistance is pegged at Y106.75, with further resistance at Y107.00, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On the downside, the dollar found support at its intraday low of Y106.38. Technical support is pegged at Y106.34. \par \par \uc2  "Some traders seem to feel the dollar relatively cheap at those levels," said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  While many traders said they think the dollar has room to fall against the yen, many are reluctant to push their luck for fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kenneth Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Tokyo said "caution should be used" below Y106.40, noting that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen on March 8 when the dollar was trading just above Y106. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y106.60, above Y106.53 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y107.15 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9061, unchanged from levels in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at $0.9043 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese interbank traders kept a close eye on movements of the Nikkei 225 stock average. While many expected weakness in Japanese share prices to be reflected in yen weakness as well, in the end, that wasn't the case. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas investors are selling Japanese shares but not the yen," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN AMRO Bank. Takano said that factor will likely limit the dollar's upside potential for now. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei 225 dipped below 16000 before ending Wednesday's session at 16044.44, down 274.29 points from Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  In the background, the yen is also benefiting from speculation that Japan's first quarter gross domestic product data due out around June 12 will show strong economic growth. Some traders are also betting that senior Japanese government officials are mulling a supplementary budget to boost their prospects in upcoming general elections. \par \par \uc2  Still, many traders expect the dollar to remain in a tight range against the yen for the rest of the week - capped by jitters over U.S. equities markets, but supported by notions that Japanese monetary authorities won't stand for a sharp appreciation in the yen. \par \par \uc2  "I think the dollar-yen will trade in a range, with a downward bias," Takano said. "If the Dow falls again, the dollar would be pushed down, but the movement won't accelerate because of fear of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the euro stuck to narrow ranges against the dollar, trading between $0.9044-$0.9075 during Wednesday's session. \par \par \uc2  Traders are awaiting the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on monetary policy expected to be announced Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there will be a rate hike," said Commerzbank's Muramatsu, adding that such an outcome could result in euro selling against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The euro's tone remains weak," Muramatsu said. \par \par \uc2  Late in Tokyo, the euro was quoted at Y96.59, up from Y96.53 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y96.90 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.4749, down from $1.4770 in New York and lower than $1.4907 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott; 813-5255-2929; arran.scott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5o02jwo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
