\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar adrift as market awaits Fed decision. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 12:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 16 (Reuters) - The dollar meandered in narrow ranges on Tuesday as the market awaited the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-making meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  While the Federal Open Market Committee was widely expected to raise U.S. interest rates by a half percentage point, traders said the market was holding its breath to see what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to say on its future policy, particularly given the fragile U.S. asset markets of late. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone expects them to do it, we expect them to do it, and it's really got to be the statement (after a rate announcement) if there's going to be any surprise," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved to and fro in a tight $0.9065-0.9105 range against the euro, consolidating about a cent off last Friday's two-week troughs around $0.92. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the greenback hovered around 109, down marginally on the day but still within shouting distance of last week's two-month peaks just above 110. \par \par \uc2  The yen was bolstered in Asia by comments from Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, who reiterated that the BOJ could end its zero-interest-rate policy when Japanese personal income clearly stopped falling. \par \par \uc2  "Hayami's comments spurred some stop-loss selling, but the amounts were not large. The moves were exaggerated by thin volumes," said Hideyuki Tsukamoto, a manager Fuji Bank manager in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Traders said business was confined largely to position adjustment ahead of the Fed decision, due to be announced at 1815 GMT. \par \par \uc2  According to a Reuters poll conducted on Friday, 27 of 29 primary dealers expected a half-point increase in the Fed's target for the federal funds rate to 6.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  "If we get a 50 basis point rate hike, it would be no shakes and I don't think there would be a huge fall-out in the dollar or U.S. assets, unless there is a frightening statement accompanying it," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read in London. \par \par \uc2  EURO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  FEARS WANE \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro had lost some of its recent lustre as wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  waned. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering on fears of such \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action had been cited as the main reason for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery from record lows below $0.89 set early this month. But traders said there was a limit to how long the euro could garner support from such a factor in the absence of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will diminish in time and you'll see a renewed bout of euro weakness going forward," said Shea at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly dipped after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke was quoted by German business daily Handelsblatt as saying he did not expect the big \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  blocs - Europe, the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to stage concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the comments were very wise or helpful and I don't know whether they were sanctioned by other members of the ECB," said Marian Bell, treasury economist at Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  "To rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage is not very helpful given it is one of the things the ECB could do if the euro started falling again." ((London Capital Markets +44-20-7542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5g00hzt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
