\par\par \b \uc2  WORLD BONDS-Any euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  short-term boost for bonds. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nigel Stephenson \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2000\par 14:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 8 (Reuters) - European government bonds would benefit from a short-term rally if the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the surprise step of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the euro, fixed income analysts said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, they said any boost to bonds would be short-lived as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not prevent a rise in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In any event, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked unlikely in the current climate. \par \par \uc2  "The risks of being ineffective appear to outweigh the potential benefits of storming in," said Alison Cottrell, chief international economist at PaineWebber in London. \par \par \uc2  With the euro plumbing new lows against the dollar last week, financial markets have been on alert for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone finance ministers meeting in Brussels on Monday said in a statement they shared a common concern about the euro's present level but made no mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they thought such a step unlikely and that, if it occurred, any impact would be short-lived and that in the end, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be no substitute for far higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Cottrell said that for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro/dollar exchange rate to be effective, the ECB would require the support of the U.S. Federal Reserve Board. However, with the Fed widely seen readying a 50 basis point hike in interest rates for later this month, such support looked unlikely. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have an initial impact on the euro and euro bonds debt as the ECB would be seen to be acting, she said. \par \par \uc2  "Initially there would be just a degree of surprise and the whole thing would get a bit of a bounce," she said. \par \par \uc2  However, with the bank's solo venture doomed to failure, the overall effect would be to hit the bank's credibility. \par \par \uc2  "Your net impact at the end of all that for bonds would be negative because you would be left with an ECB that had shot its bolt and hadn't achieved anything - which is the reason why I don't think they will do it," Cottrell said. \par \par \uc2  RATE HIKE FEARS DRIVE UP YIELDS \par \par \uc2  Expectations of higher interest rates to support the euro and squash any inflation that a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might bring have driven bond yields higher in recent weeks, particularly at the short end which is most sensitive to changes in rates. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to change that very much...I don't think the market is going to believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to be a substitute for higher interest rates so the front end still looks very vulnerable," said Cesar Molinas, European strategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  The long end would be less hard hit so the yield curve would flatten. \par \par \uc2  He said it was unlikely the ECB would move from a hands-off approach, having never openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro, to a stance of defending a set exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  He drew a parallel with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a sterilised basis, draining additional liquidity produced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to smooth out sharp yen fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  "If (the ECB) decide on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all they may wait for a sharp move of the euro towards $0.86 which is the technical support that everybody is thinking about," Molinas said. \par \par \uc2  Matt King, fixed income strategist at J.P. Morgan, saw \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an unlikely step for the ECB. The sheer scale of flows to fund corporate mergers and acquisitions would mean \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely only have a short-term impact. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro keeps going down people are going to say bonds need to back up much more because sooner or later they are going to have to hike interest rates a lot more than they thought over the next couple of years. \par \par \uc2  "On the other hand, if the euro goes up then we say they don't need to hike interest rates quite that much so bonds can rally a little bit," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said that if the euro stayed at current levels, the ECB's refinancing rate, now at 3.75 percent would rise to 5.50 percent within two years. ((London Capital Markets +44 20 7542 8682, fax +44 20 7542 5285, nigel.stephenson@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw580138z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
