\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Rises Vs Dlr, Yen On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fear \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2000\par 07:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro rose moderately against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia Monday on fears of euro-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  The fears also lifted the dollar against the yen, due to euro-yen buying which involved dollar-yen purchases in the process. \par \par \uc2  Concerns expressed last week by top European monetary officials about the recent euro weakness kept \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players alert about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Asian trading time, dealers said. Such caution nudged overseas investors and interbank players to buy the euro for the yen and dollar, dealers noted. \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to tell whether (the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today. But I'm sure its officials won't leave the weak euro as it is for long," said Takayuki Togawa, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Tokai Bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as $0.9026 and Y98.33 at one point, but later lost some of its gains to profit-taking, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Many said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if indeed implemented, would have a limited effect on the euro, as euro-bearish sentiment remains strong. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective only if they were conducted jointly by the European and U.S. central banks. Otherwise, the euro cannot get out of its current weakness easily," said Ryuichi Takami, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the euro was at $0.9015, higher than $0.8973 late Friday in New York. Tokyo markets were closed last Wednesday through Friday for holidays. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y98.16, up from Y97.43 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at Y108.89, above Y108.58 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either by E.U.-U.S. or E.U.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, is regarded as low by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players. E.U. officials apparently don't consider the current euro-weakness as serious enough to warrant joint action, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The present euro weakness is mainly due to exceptional factors such as jump in European investors' purchase of U.S. companies in the past year. The euro weakness may continue for a while, but may not be severe enough to require a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sanwa's Takami. \par \par \uc2  In speculating on the form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , players are focusing on a meeting of the European Union's finance ministers scheduled later Monday. If the ministers express concerns stronger than the ones expressed last week, that could be a sign of impending joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Euro-yen buying, which involves dollar-yen purchases, also helped the dollar to rise temporarily above Y109.00 Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said that even without the euro-yen buying, the dollar has resumed its upward trend against the yen on its own. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investors' sales of Japanese stocks to make up for losses they suffered in a volatile U.S. stock market a few weeks ago have already run their course, while there are no new factors to prompt traders to buy the yen for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As a result, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players will likely test Y110.50 in the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Until early June, when Japan's gross domestic product data for the January-March period will be released, new yen-supportive news is unlikely to emerge. The dollar is likely to be steady between Y107.00 and Y110.00 for the time being," said Tokai's Togawa. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5278, a tad up from $1.5277 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2934; takeshi.takeuchi@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates which accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture which is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw580278v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
